        "original_id": "96b779bd-4824-581c-ad84-d68540d542a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Heckscher Park, Huntington, Suffolk County, New York\n- Organizations: Heckscher Museum of Art\n- People: August Heckscher\n- Structures: Chapin Rainbow Theater\n- Topics: Park features, historic district status, public programs\n\nFacts:\n- Heckscher Park is a local park and a national historic district in Huntington, Suffolk County, New York.\n- Heckscher Park is roughly triangular in shape and has a large pond at its northwest corner.\n- Heckscher Park contains the Heckscher Museum of Art.\n- Industrialist August Heckscher established the Heckscher Museum of Art.\n- Heckscher Park also contains the Chapin Rainbow Theater.\n- The Heckscher Museum of Art offers public programs for adults, families, and children, including the \"First Friday\" concert series, gallery talks, festivals, and workshops.",
